Stocking Monsters
The table below applies to both "keyed" rooms that are occupied as well as wondering monsters. Every
level will have a table of 3 or 4 wandering monsters. Often each type of monster is limited to a specific
quadrant or section of the dungeon.

Group I: Bandit, Centipede (Giant), Dwarf, Elf, Fairy, Gnoll, Gnome, Goblin, Halfling, Insect (Giant),
Kobold, Orc, NRP (1st - 5th level Magic-User or Warrior), Pixie, Spider (Giant), Skeleton, Sprite, Zombie
Dungeon Levels 1 - 2
Group II: Beetle (Giant), Ghoul, Gargoyle, Hero, Lycanthrope, Ochre Jelly, Ogre, NRP (4th - 6th level
M-U or Warrior), Roc, Scorpion (Giant), Snake (Giant), Spectre, SuperHero, Toad (Giant), Troll, Wight
Dungeon Levels 3 - 4
Group III: Bealuwearg, Cockatrice, Dragon, Elemental, Giant, Hog (Giant), Hydra (7 headed),
Manticore, Mhrent, Mummy, NRP (Gallant w/+1 armor and magic shield; or a 5th - 9th level M-U or
Warrior), True Troll, Weasel (Giant), Wourme (Giant), Wraith, Vampire
Dungeon Levels 5 - 6

Encounter Difficulty
Encounters can be weakened or strengthened by reducing or increasing the HTK for the monster to
represent an especially feeble or cunning foe. The Referee may use an easier or harder
Group than normal (determined at random), so it is possible for a Group I monster like Dwarves to end
up on the 5th level of the dungeon. Or, to cite another example, a powerful Vampire could very easily
end up being encountered as a wandering monster on the first level of a dungeon.

