 Number Appearing - Optional
The Referee may decide that only one monster appears and need not make a dice roll.
If a) the dungeon level and b) the average experience level of the adventurers are the same as the
average Hit Dice of the monster(s) encountered, then the number appearing depends on the dungeon
level:
◦
 Levels 1 - 4 roll 1d6 for the number appearing
◦
 Levels 5 - 6 roll 1d4 for the number appearing
Exception: Monsters with 1 Hit Dice usually are encountered in groups of either 2d6 or 2d12.
If either a) the dungeon level or b) the average experience level of the adventurers are significantly
higher than the average Hit Dice of the monster(s) encountered, then roll as above, however also
multiply the number of monsters by either (a) or (b) or the average of the two.
Designer Note: These complicated mechanics are from the Arneson v. Gygax draft ruleset.
